      "body": "## Purpose\n\nFix `:nvidia: (4xB200) DeepSeek-V4.1 NVIDIA Kernels` (nightly). It has failed 12 times in a row since #64111 merged ([latest: 99485](https://buildkite.com/vllm/ci/builds/99485#01a1a039-4070-49ba-bf82-733112dd7dba)):\n\n```\nFAILED models/deepseek_v41/nvidia/specialized_decode/test_kernels.py::test_engram_wkv_prefetch_matches_inline[False]\nFAILED models/deepseek_v41/nvidia/specialized_decode/test_kernels.py::test_engram_wkv_prefetch_matches_inline[True]\nAttributeError: '_Mxfp8Linear' object has no attribute 'params_dtype'\n```\n\n**Root cause:** #64111 changed `FlashInferCutedslMxfp8LinearKernel.apply_weights` (`vllm/model_executor/kernels/linear/mxfp8/flashinfer.py`) to take the output dtype of unquantized inputs from `layer.params_dtype` instead of `x.dtype`. Real vLLM linear layers always set `params_dtype`, but the hand-built `_Mxfp8Linear` stand-in in this test did not.\n\n**Why #64111's CI didn't catch it:** the step is `optional: true` (nightly only), so it never runs on PRs, and its source triggers don't include `vllm/model_executor/kernels/linear/mxfp8/`.\n\n**Fix:** set `params_dtype = torch.bfloat16` on the stand-in, as a real linear layer would. The test feeds bf16 inputs, so the kernel's output dtype is the same as before #64111.\n\n**Not a duplicate:** no open PR touches this test or stub.\n\n## Test Plan\n\nNot run locally (needs B200 GPUs). The step is nightly-only, so it will be confirmed by the next nightly after merge, or by a selected-step run of `dsv41-nvidia-kernels-4xb200` on this PR.\n\n## Notes\n\nAI assistance (Claude Code) was used; reviewed by the submitter.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
